<p>Lebanon and Israel are set to hold talks in Washington next week, in what the Financial Times described as the first direct negotiations between the two countries in more than four decades. Lebanese officials said the meeting is scheduled for Tuesday in the United States, and reports said preliminary contacts have already taken place ahead of the U.S.-brokered discussions. That channel is notable because Lebanon and Israel remain formally at war, and recent cross-border fighting tied to the wider Middle East conflict has sharply raised tensions. Israel said the upcoming talks will not cover a ceasefire with Hezbollah, while Lebanese President Joseph Aoun has repeatedly signaled his readiness for direct talks with Israel since Hezbollah opened fire on Israel on March 2, drawing Lebanon further into the regional war, according to Le Monde. Even with those limits, the planned meeting offers a rare opening for dialogue after decades without direct negotiations. It gives both sides a chance to test whether a narrowly focused diplomatic process can lower tensions.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4lYWvawxt5K9QUaOSmnfxCHhcDf5IRW33qHl5wet51W-jqzsUKXzCtAziC69926H4cm0EQT7EEyCTfWvvvaXqRGRMOmrjcqCQ9Dar_wsUQLIRYq7bwmQT7poPRNtcVSWPPpqSTSxLd9AoL_50E0LLJE_qVkY3r4Aahi3J1A2ady7cTMXhJpfeYo9Rct8EQQZzyTP3gDyG_df-JjHR2UshkD-MklSk0TV3MarX29NMALqlYfz53kEY7LzGA' alt='Lebanese President Joseph Aoun gestures to journalists at the Presidential Palace, in Baabda, east of Beirut, Lebanon, Wednesday, on May 21, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>U.S. mediation: The United States is brokering the discussions, with Washington hosting preliminary talks between Lebanese and Israeli officials.</li><li>Agenda limits: Israel said on Friday that the Washington meeting with Lebanon&#x27;s government will not include a ceasefire with Hezbollah.</li><li>First contact: Lebanon said an initial contact with Israel had already taken place before the formal U.S.-brokered talks, suggesting preparations are already under way.</li><li>Rare format: The Financial Times said the meeting would mark the first direct negotiations between Lebanon and Israel in more than 40 years.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israel: Israeli officials said the Washington meeting will not include talks over a ceasefire with Hezbollah, signaling that the agenda will stay narrow. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/lebanon-says-talks-with-israel-scheduled-for-tuesday-in-the-us_6752301_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Lebanese President Joseph Aoun: Aoun has repeatedly said he is open to direct talks with Israel since March 2, showing that Lebanon&#x27;s presidency sees dialogue as an option despite the conflict. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/lebanon-says-talks-with-israel-scheduled-for-tuesday-in-the-us_6752301_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>United States: Washington is hosting and brokering the talks, framing the meeting as a structured diplomatic opening rather than a one-off contact. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/lebanon-says-first-contact-with-israel-held-ahead-of-u-s-brokered-talks/article70849016.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/ffef195c-8b3c-48fc-bddd-64036880dc6f'>Lebanon and Israel agree to talks in Washington next week</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/lebanon-says-talks-with-israel-scheduled-for-tuesday-in-the-us_6752301_4.html'>Lebanon says talks with Israel scheduled for Tuesday in the US</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/lebanon-says-first-contact-with-israel-held-ahead-of-us-brokered-talks/article70849016.ece'>Lebanon says first contact with Israel held ahead of U.S.-brokered talks</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://aje.news/8znvvy?update=4480481'>Preliminary talks between Lebanese and Israeli officials are pl